From 21c26ff50d1a0a38668cd07855724bb87311cb24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:54:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] tests: build the T6050 paths that #30 adds

Five host tests compile production bodies that #30 extends for T6050
and stop compiling or matching on its head:
- test_nvme_adoption and test_smp_handoff_gate: nvme_init() and
  kboot_boot() now name T6050, and kboot_boot() calls dapf_init().
  Define T6050 and stub dapf_init() beside the existing stubs.
- test_m3_defaults_optout: payload_run() names T6050 for the live ANS
  session hand-off. Define it.
- test_universal_boot: the stage 1 config block now reads boot_spec and
  kernel (an appended next stage takes only the proxy window). Declare
  both, and add the cases #30 introduces: with boot_spec or an appended
  kernel set, a configured target adds neither a chainload target nor
  its ESP hint, and a chainload= line is kept rather than refused. T6050
  joins the chip list of the configured-target cases.
- test_t8103_inherited_reservation ends its block at the T8140 heap
  check, which is now "T8140 || T6050" with a comment line before it.
  Match both forms.

integration/aurora passes all five before and after; on #30's head
they fail without this.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 tests/python/test_m3_defaults_optout.py          |  1 +
 tests/python/test_nvme_adoption.py               |  1 +
 tests/python/test_smp_handoff_gate.py            |  2 ++
 tests/python/test_t8103_inherited_reservation.py |  4 +++-
 tests/python/test_universal_boot.py              | 14 +++++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

